# we use Shopify as our ecommerce platform
{%- comment -%}
  Caution! Read https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/seo/editing-robots-txt
  before you change this file.

  Three customizations live here. Read the notes before you edit.

  1. LINE BREAKS (tracker task 39). Every directive is built by hand from
     `.directive` and `.value`, and each {% raw %}{% %}{% endraw %} tag sits flush against its
     neighbour so the literal newlines survive. Do NOT print a drop directly
     ({% raw %}{{ rule }}{% endraw %}, {% raw %}{{ group.user_agent }}{% endraw %}) and do NOT add {% raw %}{{- ... -}}{% endraw %}
     whitespace markers. The previous version did both and rendered
     "User-agent: *Disallow: /a/downloads/-/*" on the live site.
     robots.txt cannot be previewed on an unpublished theme, so always check
     https://jalg.me/robots.txt right after you publish.

  2. POLICIES. The `unless` drops Shopify's default `Disallow: /policies/`
     so policy pages stay crawlable. PRE-EXISTING - do not remove.

  3. AI CRAWLERS (tracker task 8, GEO audit section 3). Approved 2026-07-06:
     both tiers allowed - the citation tier that earns AI citations, and the
     training tier that feeds long-term model knowledge. To opt out of
     training later, change that group's `Allow: /` to `Disallow: /`.

     A named bot obeys ONLY its own group, never `User-agent: *`. So each AI
     group replays the `*` rules from `ai_disallows` below. That is built from
     Shopify's own `*` group, so when Shopify adds a path, the AI groups get
     it too. Nothing to maintain by hand.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- for group in robots.default_groups -%}
{%- if group.user_agent.value == '*' -%}
{%- capture ai_disallows -%}
{% for rule in group.rules %}{% unless rule.directive == 'Disallow' and rule.value == '/policies/' %}{{ rule.directive }}: {{ rule.value }}
{% endunless %}{% endfor %}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor %}

{% for group in robots.default_groups %}{{ group.user_agent.directive }}: {{ group.user_agent.value }}
{% for rule in group.rules %}{% unless rule.directive == 'Disallow' and rule.value == '/policies/' %}{{ rule.directive }}: {{ rule.value }}
{% endunless %}{% endfor %}{% if group.sitemap != blank %}{{ group.sitemap.directive }}: {{ group.sitemap.value }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor -%}
